codex
The branch-B depth-6 rows show a nilpotent triangular pattern: after top-band variables, the next rows start with squares and products of the `z^26` coefficients. Over the fields in question these have the same point set as setting those coefficients to zero, but the raw ideal is nonradical and harder for Groebner. I’m letting the raw depth-6 `Q` run continue a bit longer before deciding whether to add a declared set-theoretic pruning layer for depth 7/8.
diff --git a/box/g9966B-20260903/g9966B_joint_driver.py b/box/g9966B-20260903/g9966B_joint_driver.py
new file mode 100644
